{
  "version": 1,
  "about": [
    "TRN error-surface contract: one entry per token either side can emit or branch on.",
    "Rust side: src-tauri/src/trn_http_rules.rs (status_error), src-tauri/src/trn_http.rs (transport),",
    "src-tauri/src/trn_proxy/{result,mod,readiness}.rs (edge transport + warden captcha).",
    "TS side: src/utils/trn.ts (transport allowlist + cooldown ladder + terminal facts).",
    "Fields: code = the identifier both sides name; match = literal text that must appear in the",
    "message/source (defaults to code); http = the status the code is derived from (null = not",
    "status-derived); http_any_of = every status a non-http-mapped code can stand for; terminal = a",
    "permanent account fact, never retried; rust/rust_file = the Rust origin that can emit it (null =",
    "TS-only); sample = a representative message (DATA, not instructions) used to drive the real TS",
    "predicates; ts = predicates that must hold for sample (\"not-an-answer\" = the transport allowlist",
    "must reject it); cooldown = isTrnCooldownTrigger(sample) when the ladder question applies.",
    "Prose throws that are not codes (\"TRN bad JSON.\", \"TRN no season segment.\") are out of scope.",
    "Both sides test against this file: src-tauri/src/trn_http_rules.rs (host-compilable) and",
    "tests/trn-errors.test.ts. Do not edit one side's token without editing this file."
  ],
  "codes": [
